adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset, it evaluates to `undefined`. If the request also omits the header (so `req.headers[...]` is also `undefined`), then `undefined !== undefined` is `false`, meaning the request is treated as authenticated and proceeds. There is no prior guard that the secret must be configured. The note about non-constant-time comparison is also accurate (string equality is not guaranteed constant-time), but the main verifiable issue is the authentication bypass when the secret env var is missing.
